From 8a973e374d5dd12fcfc560eed6fe6002660f97aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:08:49 +0000
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: add xRX500 SoC dtsi and EASY350 ANYWAN board

Add the xRX500 SoC device tree include and the Intel EASY350 ANYWAN
(GRX350 reference board) DTS.

The dtsi describes the SoC as brought up on real hardware: cpuintc +
GIC, the CGU clock controller, the RCU syscon (reset controller and
GPHY reset provider), serial, the SSX4 localbus with the EBU NAND
controller window at 0x17c00000 (chip-select 1), the two GSWIP-3.0
switch instances (gswl@1c000000, gswr@1a000000), the GSWIP MDIO bus,
the GPHY firmware loader node, the four central DMA controllers, and
the CBM (central buffer manager) node with its twelve register
windows - the disabled-at-SoC-scope nodes are enabled per board.

Based on the initial xrx500.dtsi from the 2018 intel-mips submission
by Songjun Wu <songjun.wu@linux.intel.com>:

  https://lore.kernel.org/all/20180803030237.3366-1-songjun.wu@linux.intel.com/

extended during FRITZ!Box 7560 bring-up with the nodes listed above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
